Why isn't that made clear when it clearly states "written in Perl"?

Perl is a script language, which means you will _always_ need an
interpreter to run a Perl script. This is no different under Linux, only
that you'll hardly find a Linux system which hasn't Perl support
installed by default, whereas under Windows you always need to install 
it yourself. That isn't the programmer's fault, though, nor that of Perl.

I don't really want to argue with you, I'm just not sure whether you've 
understood the concept of script languages and/or platform-independency.


Having said that, the script gives me an error in Windows because the 
"getpwuid" call isn't implemented (latest ActivePerl release). If I 
replace it, everything runs fine. I like the program very much so far, I 
only haven't played enough games yet for the analyses to be truly 
interesting.

Thank you for sharing, Markus!

